<title>BANGLADESH: Dhaka bourse signs deal to automate trading.</title>
<headline>Dhaka bourse signs deal to automate trading.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dhaka Stock Exchange (DSE) on Thursday signed $2.0 million deal with Tandem Computers International Inc for the automation of stock trading, a DSE statement said.</p>
<p>It said the company would &quot;install a main frame computer with a fully automated trading system.&quot; The system will enable brokers to trade from &quot;other locations&quot; in the city, it said but gave no other details.</p>
<p>The statement, however, said the system would be operational by September, 1997.</p>
</text>
